PKGCHK(1)

# NAME

pkgchk - audit installed package objects

# SYNOPSIS

*pkgchk* {-l | -d | -a} *--canonical-store* _path_ \\
	*--managed-target* _identity_ *--state-store* _identity_ \\
	*--root-view* _identity_ *--state-backend* _identity_ \\
	*--publication-domain* _identity_ [-r _root-dir_] [-v] [_package_ ...]

*pkgchk* {-V | -h}

# DESCRIPTION

*pkgchk* is the reference frontend for *libpkgaudit*(3).  It opens one
existing canonical native installed-state store through libpkgstate-posix,
converts the immutable snapshot into the independent audit model, observes
the selected target root, and presents the resulting facts.

The state store is opened read-only against the exact caller-supplied target
binding.  *pkgchk* never initializes a store, publishes or repairs a
generation, imports a historical database, or reconstructs missing state.

If no package names are supplied, all installed packages are audited.
Exactly one audit mode is required.

# OPTIONS

*-l*, *--links*
	Check symlink resolution and ownership.

*-d*, *--disappeared*
	Check object presence and durable directory/non-directory class.

*-a*, *--audit*
	Run all checks.

*-c* _path_, *--canonical-store*=_path_
	Open the existing canonical native installed-state store at _path_.

*--managed-target*=_identity_
	Managed package-target identity bound to the state store.

*--state-store*=_identity_
	Durable installed-state store identity.

*--root-view*=_identity_
	Logical target root-view identity.

*--state-backend*=_identity_
	Installed-state backend identity.

*--publication-domain*=_identity_
	Publication and locking-domain identity.

*-r* _root-dir_, *--root*=_root-dir_
	Inspect objects beneath _root-dir_.  The default is /.

*-v*
	Increase presentation detail.  Repeatable.

*-V*, *--version*
	Print version information and exit.

*-h*, *--help*
	Print usage and exit.

# EXIT STATUS

*0*
	The audit completed without integrity findings.

*1*
	The audit completed and reported integrity findings.

*2*
	Command usage, installed state, filesystem observation, or backend
	contract prevented a complete audit.

Ownership relations are advisory and do not by themselves change the
exit status.

# DESIGN

libpkgstate and libpkgstate-posix are linked by this executable, not by
libpkgaudit.  Severity, diagnostic text, verbosity, and exit status are
frontend policy.

# SEE ALSO

*libpkgaudit*(3), *pkgstate-check*(1)

